# trivy vulnerability ignore list.
#
# Each entry is a CVE ID with a comment block explaining why it is accepted
# here rather than fixed -- package, reachability, accept date, and the
# condition under which the ignore should be removed. Scoped to one CVE at
# a time; never a whole package or severity band.
#
# CVE-2026-81726 -- nltk 3.10.3, HIGH, path traversal in nltk's model-artifact
# download APIs (nltk.download() / Downloader). No fixed nltk release exists
# yet. nltk is transitive only, pulled in by llama-index-core==0.14.12 (see
# uv.lock); the floor at nltk>=3.10.3 in pyproject.toml's
# constraint-dependencies is for two earlier CVEs (CVE-2026-79675,
# CVE-2026-78680), not a direct dependency. CogSynDelta code never imports
# nltk: `grep -rn "nltk" src/ scripts/ tests/` finds no matches, so the
# vulnerable download path is unreachable in this repo.
# Accepted 2026-09-03. Remove when nltk publishes a fixed version;
# `uv lock --upgrade-package nltk`.
CVE-2026-81726
